error[ffi_call_shape]: `stdio.h` declares `stdin` as an object of type `FILE *`, not a function: clang read the header, and the call this declaration implies does not fit it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-152-a-pointer-object-declared-as-a-function.hero:12:5
     |
  12 |     function stdin() -> ptr  #~ ffi_call_shape
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: an object can hold another value at the next read, so no group member binds one, and a `constant` refuses it (§4.19): a function of the program's own returns it, written in a header beside this file and bound by `extern` naming that header like any function, `static inline FILE *hero_stdin(void) { return stdin; }`
